# Admin List Usability

Admin management pages are work surfaces. Prefer dense, comparable rows over card grids when users scan, sort, compare, or act on records.

- Default admin index pages to tables or table-like responsive rows, not unrelated boxed cards.
- Every listed record must expose its allowed primary actions in the row: view/details when a detail route exists, edit when update is allowed, delete/remove when delete is allowed, and domain-specific actions such as registrations/history when relevant.
- Do not require horizontal scrolling to reach row actions. On desktop, keep an actions column visible; on mobile, stack each row with visible labels and actions under the primary identifier.
- The primary identifier should link to the safest default destination: detail/view if it exists, otherwise edit when update is allowed.
- Empty states must say what is empty and, when create is allowed, expose the create action.
